During an interview on NBC's "Meet the Press," Araghchi addressed reports of potential US bombing of Iran following the midterm elections. He said, "We are now ready for a war, but we are still trying to find a diplomatic solution."

Araghchi emphasized that Iran is willing to engage in negotiations, but also prepared for any challenges, "even if it means fighting a war to the end."

Iran had previously submitted a proposal to the US through Qatar, suggesting reopening the Hormuz Strait within seven days to restore normal shipping in the global oil transportation route. However, Trump rejected the proposal and claimed Iran was desperate to reach an agreement because they had suffered too much.

Araghchi stated that Iran is still willing to negotiate, but the US must meet certain conditions, including unfreezing Iranian assets and allowing the sale of oil. He reiterated that these were not new demands but commitments made by the US previously.

The US had signed a memorandum of understanding with Iran in June, but the agreement broke down after both sides launched attacks. Araghchi also pointed out that Iran is not concerned about the US midterm elections but rather its national interests.

On September 26, the Iranian Revolutionary Guard claimed to have detained a US Navy unmanned underwater vehicle (UUV) in the Hormuz Strait. The claim was made by Tasnim News Agency on Telegram, stating that the vehicle was a Remus 600, which has been handed over to experts for data extraction. The US Navy did not immediately respond to the request for comment.

Araghchi also announced on September 25 at the UN headquarters in New York that Iran had submitted a proposal to reopen the Hormuz Strait to the US through Qatar. If the US took necessary actions based on this proposal, the Strait could be reopened within seven days, restoring normal shipping. However, the US "Wall Street Journal" reported that Trump rejected the Iranian proposal and told his aides that he might resume bombing Iran after the US midterm elections.

Araghchi clarified that the US has not yet formally rejected the Iranian proposal. He emphasized that only negotiations can break the deadlock. As part of the agreement, Iran is willing to reopen the Strait, but the US must meet certain conditions, including unfreezing Iranian assets and allowing the sale of oil.

US Ambassador to the UN, Michael Waltz, criticized Iran's latest proposal as a "fake gesture" that the US cannot accept. He stated that Trump will retain all options.

Regarding potential US attacks on Iran, the Iranian military spokesman, Amirali Hajizadeh, stated that the Iranian armed forces are fully prepared and will make every effort to counter any attacks.
