2026-10-05 23:26:52 - agent_core.graph - DEBUG - script attempt 2 content: According to NBC, Iran's Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi expressed that Iran is now prepared for a potential war with the US after President Trump publicly rejected Iran's proposal for reopening the Strait of Hormuz. However, Araghchi has not given up on diplomatic efforts.

During his interview on NBC's "Meet the Press," Araghchi said, "We are ready for a war, but we are still trying to find a diplomatic solution." He emphasized that if attacked again, Iran would stand firm, "even if it means a war to the end."

Araghchi also stated that Iran is still willing to resolve the issue through diplomacy, "now it is up to President Trump to make the choice."

Last week, Iran submitted a proposal to reopen the Strait of Hormuz as part of a peace agreement, requesting its reopening within seven days. However, Trump rejected the proposal, stating that Iran is desperate to reach an agreement because they have lost too much.

Araghchi clarified that Iran has not received a formal rejection of the proposal from the US yet. He reiterated that Iran is willing to reopen the Strait of Hormuz as part of a deal, but in exchange, the US must release frozen Iranian funds and assets, and allow Iran to sell oil.

The Iranian Revolutionary Guard Corps claimed to have detained a US Navy underwater drone (UUV) in the Strait of Hormuz. The Revolutionary Guard quoted by Tasnim News Agency said the drone is a Remus 600 and has been handed over to experts for data extraction. The US Navy did not immediately respond to a request for comment.

